  "verbalization": "Nobotanin A is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways, with FaDu as a common target in all three evidence chains. The drug is linked to FaDu, which is a target of both (3R,3aR,6R,7aR)-6-hydroxy-3,6-dimethyl-3a,4,7,7a-tetrahydro-3H-1-benzofuran-2,5-dione and Heneicosane. These compounds are both targets of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2) pathway. The final scores across all three paths are consistent, indicating a strong, albeit indirect, relationship between Nobotanin A and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence supports a role for Nobotanin A in modulating PRC2 activity, potentially through the inhibition of its core component, EZH2. The mechanism is supported by the presence of multiple targets in the pathway, and the shared interaction with the complex suggests a plausible biological role in epigenetic regulation.",
